# Activity 1: How the Internet Works Students simulate the interaction between a browser, server, and database to understand how requests are processed and responses are returned. 
Activity 1: How the Internet Works
📌 Objective

To understand how a browser, server, and database communicate through the Internet using requests and responses.

🛠️ Technologies / Concepts
Web Browser
Web Server
Database
HTTP/HTTPS
Request and Response Cycle
📖 Activity Description

Students will simulate the interaction between a browser, server, and database to understand how requests are processed and responses are returned.

🔄 Workflow
The browser sends a request to the server.
The server receives and processes the request.
The server retrieves the required information from the database.
The database returns the requested data to the server.
The server sends a response to the browser.
The browser displays the result to the user.
💻 Example Scenario

A user opens a webpage to check student marks.

Browser: Requests student marks.
Server: Processes the request.
Database: Returns the stored marks.
Server: Sends the response.
Browser: Displays the marks.

Example output:

Student Name: Student A
Marks: 85/100
Status: Success

📝 Tasks
Identify the roles of the browser, server, and database.
Draw a diagram showing the request-and-response cycle.
Explain how the browser communicates with the server.
Describe the role of the database.
Demonstrate the process using a role-play or a simple program.
